-- title:
--   Per-class double-coset bound for twisted orbital integrals
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, let $\nu_{Z_L}$ be a Haar measure on the idèle units $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ (with its Borel structure), let $D$ be an [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28), i.e. a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ which is continuous in each element and extends the action on $L$, let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, let $S$ be a finite set of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$, let $\varphi_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adèles and a family $\varphi_{S,v}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ be given, let $H$ be a closed subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ whose elements are exactly the $h$ with $h_{10} = h_{01} = 0$ and $\sigma_D(h)h^{-1}$ central, where $\sigma_D$ is the entrywise action of $D(\sigma)$, and let $\mu_H$ be a right-invariant Haar measure on $H$. Then for every finite set $T$ of primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$ and every choice $w_v$ of a prime of $\mathcal{O}_L$ above each $v$ there are $C \ge 0$ and $A \in \mathbb{N}$ with the following property. Let $\rho_v \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ for all $v$, and let $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adèles satisfy `IsSemiLocalFactorization` for the set $S \cup T$ with archimedean factor $\varphi_a$ and semi-local data equal, at $v \in T$, to the indicator of the double coset $\mathcal{K}_v \, a_v \, \mathcal{K}_v$, where $\mathcal{K}_v$ is the integral units subset `semiLocalIntegralSet` of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ and $a_v$ is the semi-local component of the image of $\rho_v$ under [`AdelicDock.localEmbed`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L97), and to $\varphi_{S,v}$ off $T$; that is, $\varphi_a$ is an arch test factor, $\varphi_f$ a finite test factor, each of these local functions a semi-local test function, $\varphi_f(h)$ equals the product over $v \in S \cup T$ of the local values whenever all components of $h$ outside $S \cup T$ are integral and vanishes otherwise, and $\varphi(g) = \varphi_a(g_\infty)\varphi_f(g_f)$. Then for every $t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with $t_{10} = t_{01} = 0$ and $N_{L/K}(t_{00}/t_{11}) \ne 1$, the lower Lebesgue integral over the quotient of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ by the orbit relation of $H$, taken with respect to [`HaarQuotient.measure`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L28) for `adelicGLHaar` and $\mu_H$, of the inner $\nu_{Z_L}$-integral in $z$ of $\lVert \varphi(q^{-1} \, t \, \sigma_D(z q)) \rVert$ (with $q$ a chosen representative, $t$ viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and $z$ as a central scalar) is at most $C \prod_{v \in T} m_v^{1/2} (1 + \log m_v)^A$, where $m_v$ is the real number given by the `semiLocalHaar` measure of that double coset at $v$.
--
--   This is the analytic estimate bounding a single unweighted hyperbolic (regular semisimple, non-norm-one) class term in the twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ by the square root of the volume of the Hecke double coset, times a power of its logarithm, uniformly in the class and in the double coset. It feeds the combined bound [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_sum_lintegral_orbital_add_weightedOrbital_doubleCoset_le_mul_prod_rpow_measure`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_sum_lintegral_orbital_add_weightedOrbital_doubleCoset_le_mul_prod_rpow_measure), where the class terms and the weighted terms are summed.
